10. Challenges & Limitations



Filament panel components rely on Livewire, making automated browser-level testing require additional setup (e.g. Dusk)

Database seeding required before each test run to ensure consistent data state

Referential integrity (FK) constraints not enforced at application layer for category deletion

No existing test coverage in the repository — all test cases written from scratch



11. Conclusion & Recommendations



The Inventory Management System core test suite now passes all documented test cases. Authentication access, product/category/supplier setup, purchase and inventory records, loan status updates, and user model behavior all pass in the automated PHPUnit run.



Priority Fixes

Add validation tests for required fields on Product, Supplier, and Purchase models to guard against incomplete data entry.

D01 & D02 resolved: Role records are created before assignRole() in the role-related UserModel tests.

General Recommendations

Write PHPUnit unit tests for Product and Stock models (see attached test files)

Write feature tests for authentication and CRUD routes

Configure phpunit.xml to use SQLite in-memory database for faster isolated tests

Integrate automated testing in a CI pipeline (e.g. GitHub Actions)
